{"t": 1794116095.9019985, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "*[checkout] PaymentGatewayErrors \u2014 root cause found, fix ready*\n\n*What's paging:* OnCall alert AG-7731 \u2014 gateway 4xx rate 38% for service=checkout since 07:41 UTC (severity critical).\n\n*Root cause:* The payment gateway switched to API version `2026-11` (\"strict amounts\") at 07:41 UTC. It now requires `amount` as an integer in minor units (cents). `checkout/gateway.py` was still sending a decimal EUR amount, so charges are rejected:\n`400 {\"error\":\"invalid_amount\",\"message\":\"amount must be an integer in minor units (cents), got 12.34\"}` (Loki, app=checkout)\n\n*Fix:* `charge_payload()` now converts EUR to integer cents (12.34 -> 1234) using `Decimal` with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, avoiding float artifacts (e.g. 0.1+0.2 -> 30 cents, not 30.000000000000004). Field name/currency unchanged. Verified locally: 12.34->1234, 19.99->1999, 1.005->101.\n\n*Next:* deploy checkout, then confirm the 4xx rate drops and AG-7731 resolves. If any caller passes non-EUR amounts, they still need their own minor-unit handling."}, "ok": true}
